            <ArticleTitle>Acute neck pain referred to the surgeon: Lemierre's syndrome as a differential diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e132-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1308/003588412X13171221589414</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lemierre's syndrome is usually reported in the young and in fit individuals. We report a case of an 81-year-old woman who presented with thrombophlebitis of the internal jugular vein with a pulmonary embolism.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
